# Line-ending normalization — M-HRD-04 / Phase 21 hardening.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: the CSP `script-src` directive pins a SHA-256 hash of the
# single inline boot <script> in ApStatsForOpenWrt/Components/App.razor. The browser
# hashes the EXACT bytes of the rendered inline script; the Razor compiler emits those
# bytes with whatever line endings the on-disk source has at compile time. With
# core.autocrlf=true and NO .gitattributes, App.razor checks out CRLF on Windows but
# LF in the Linux container build — diverging the hash and silently breaking CSP
# enforcement (and the Blazor circuit) in exactly one environment.
#
# Fix (RESEARCH Pitfall 1): normalize ALL text files to LF on disk on every platform.
# The hash is also LF-normalized in both the middleware source and the ArchitectureTest
# (CspScriptHashTests) so the pinned value is platform-deterministic regardless of
# checkout state. After adding this file, a one-time `git add --renormalize .` re-stages
# already-checked-out files with LF.

# Default: treat every file as text, auto-detect, and force LF on checkout (every OS).
* text=auto eol=lf

# The hash-relevant file — pinned explicitly (belt + braces over the wildcard above).
*.razor text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize (corrupts the bytes). Scanned from support/ and
# wwwroot/lib/: vendored fonts, images, the AdminLTE zip, and the SQLite DB on /data.
*.png   -text
*.ico   -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
*.ttf   -text
*.eot   -text
*.otf   -text
*.zip   -text
*.gz    -text
*.db    -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.gif   -text
*.webp  -text
*.pdf   -text
